IfcOpenShell 0.8.5 for the browser, and what it needs (BIM-Personal V177)
===========================================================================

These files are third-party programs, unchanged, kept apart from BIM-Personal's own code (Apache-2.0). The app loads
them only when a model is saved as IFC, inside a separate Python worker, and talks to them only by messages. The app
opens, edits and saves without them. docs/research/research-ifcopenshell-app.md (the owner's decision D1, 2026-11-13).

ifcopenshell-0.8.5-cp313-cp313-pyodide_2025_0_wasm32.whl
  IfcOpenShell, https://ifcopenshell.org, built for WebAssembly by the IfcOpenShell project and published at
  https://github.com/IfcOpenShell/wasm-wheels (tag v0.8.5). IfcOpenShell's own code is LGPL-3.0-or-later
  (COPYING.LESSER, which adds permissions to COPYING, the GPL-3.0). Its compiled module also contains:
    - CGAL, https://www.cgal.org: packages under GPL-3.0-or-later (3D Boolean Operations on Nef Polyhedra, Convex
      Decomposition of Polyhedra, 2D Arrangements, Polygon Mesh Processing, 2D Straight Skeleton and Polygon
      Offsetting) and under LGPL-3.0-or-later (the kernel, number types);
    - Open CASCADE Technology, https://dev.opencascade.org: LGPL-2.1 with Open CASCADE's exception;
    - GMP and MPFR, https://gmplib.org and https://www.mpfr.org: LGPL-3.0-or-later;
    - Boost, https://www.boost.org: Boost Software License 1.0.
  Because of the GPL parts, this file as a whole is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
  (COPYING). Its source: https://github.com/IfcOpenShell/IfcOpenShell (tag v0.8.5; the build is nix/build-all.py
  with --wasm, which names each library's version and source), https://github.com/CGAL/cgal,
  https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT.

shapely-2.0.7-cp313-cp313-pyemscripten_2025_0_wasm32.whl
  Shapely, BSD-3-Clause (its dist-info/licenses/LICENSE.txt), Pyodide 0.29.5's build; it contains GEOS,
  https://libgeos.org, LGPL-2.1. Source: https://github.com/shapely/shapely, https://github.com/libgeos/geos.

